#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:5
#: 803e12b3c0a64615bb2fdf03071f9d73
msgid "Takeoff"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:7
#: 7e74221419424da7bcdbea70c423b941
msgid "Taking the plane off can be accomplished in many ways: Rolling Takeoff, Hand Launch, Bungee, or VTOL (Vertical Takeoff and Landing) if a :ref:`quadplane-support`. And it can be done manually or automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:10
#: d736fdd500be45b4b6ea75ed3ac69721
msgid "Rolling Takeoff"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:12
#: d3f208c21a704558a5a0e5a60a112cf7
msgid "In this case, the plane has landing gear with steerable nose gear, usually coupled to the rudder control and the plane is usually launched from a smooth grass or paved surface (see the `Ground Steering parameters <https://ardupilot.org/plane/docs/parameters.html#steer2srv-parameters>`__ . Once aligned nose into the wind, throttle is gradually increased to takeoff value (usually full throttle) while the aircraft direction is controlled by rudder. Once sufficient airspeed to lift off is obtained, slight up elevator will rotate the nose to climb attitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:14
#: c99082793524452a8dbeab560239c353
msgid "MANUAL or FBWA modes are most commonly used during takeoffs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:16
#: 7142b16cdb614f75aab1ce0155a7fc33
msgid "For automatic takeoffs see :ref:`automatic-takeoff` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:19
#: 78da3709718c43ed954108474a9707bc
msgid "Hand Launch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:21
#: fff8e17f16c245859dc6e56184183791
msgid "Many planes do not have landing gear, or a smooth runway is not available. Hand launching is a very common takeoff method, but also can be very frustrating if not setup and executed properly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:23
#: 2db29673c36042be917ee146ac90fd6a
msgid "The keys to a successful hand launch are :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:25
#: 2ec7d90ed0104a3ca56936ad0985754b
msgid ":ref:`Proper CG <guide-center-of-gravity>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:26
#: e3cd2dc82e464326bf7337c62f2fc6c3
msgid "Having flying surfaces centered and neutral at neutral RC stick positions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:27
#: c99c42b9c68b404fbcf76df7a64bd209
msgid "Having the \"level\" calibration setup such that the level horizon (0 deg pitch) in FBWA mode results in the wing chord line being a few degrees positive, which will result in a positive angle of attack in \"level\" flight, the normally cruising attitude for a plane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:28
#: bb8a6ca66a94417c804b0794fbecfb95
msgid "Using FBWA mode or :ref:`automatic-takeoff`. While launching in MANUAL can be done, using a stabilized mode will eliminate a lot of pilot effort to overcome trim issues (see Tip at end of this page). If using FBWA mode, a few degrees of up elevator (~10%) during the launch will result in an automatic climb. Add this via a switch or stick pressure. Do not change TX trim positions used during RC calibration since it affects all other modes of flight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:29
#: e8b57a4d1cb1489984572b1c6b152eab
msgid "Throttle up and firmly throw the plane level directly into the wind, not nose pointed up. Common mistakes are pointing the nose up, throwing it toward the ground, or rotating your wrist like a football throw. In the first second or so, the plane has low airspeed and the flying surfaces have no authority to correct non-level attitude until it accelerates to flying speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:32
#: 8f6731249913439caf8d4f0a8beaa2d6
msgid "Videos of hand launches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:39
#: d5ee86c48d694dafb20f2aca28e93c09
msgid "Bungee"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:41
#: c96872eebee74b35be16233d4fb8b821
msgid "Bungee launching involves using an elastic band, stretched and attached to the plane, in order to provide a catapult-like takeoff."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:47
#: 8ab183bc324643909348800f9a1634c0
msgid "This is commonly used for very heavy or very high stall speed planes for launching. A tutorial on building and using a bungee launcher is `here <https://www.rcgroups.com/forums/showthread.php?1459906>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:51
#: b753d86b35ec41e58fabf81f9a689523
msgid "VTOL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:53
#: 661704dfd1bb488692bee2386889120a
msgid "Perhaps the easiest of all takeoffs, it does require that the plane be a VTOL capable :ref:`QuadPlane <quadplane-support>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:55
#: acc084109d714b02891398b36e9bd926
msgid "While not necessary for a successful launch, enabling :ref:`SERVO_AUTO_TRIM<SERVO_AUTO_TRIM>` will automatically trim the plane during stabilized operations, such that switching to MANUAL or ACRO mode later will have an in-trim plane automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/takeoff-landingpage.rst:57
#: a1a62fe56461412fbf5ca63a5247c98a
msgid "The default PIDs usually will be acceptable for most planes for their first launch. However, powerful, small flying wings will sometimes wobble in pitch at high throttle climb-outs and can benefit from initially setting ``PTCH2SRV_P`` to half its default value. These can be optimized later manually or using AUTOTUNE mode. See :ref:`tuning-quickstart`"
msgstr ""
